= Appendix B: glossary without gatekeeping

*Ollama.* Local model host. Lets large language models run as services on your computer instead of a distant chat website.

*FastAPI.* The Python web layer that serves the Classic interface and JSON APIs on port 8000 in the default story.

*EPUB.* A common ebook file shape used by many readers and many publishing paths.

*DOCX.* Microsoft Word style document. Editors and some tools love it.

*Markdown.* Plain text with light markup. GitHub readers know it. Writers love how small and durable it feels.

*Pipeline.* Plan, write, polish, export as a serious sequence instead of vibes.

*One pass expansion.* A project term for certain expand and export paths that aim at long targets across multiple model calls.

*JSON packs.* Editable data that shapes prompts and polish behavior without recompiling the entire application.

*Lexical chain.* Advanced integration pathway for deeper text tooling. Treat it as power user territory.

*Smoke test.* An automated happy path that proves packaging is not a wish.

