= Appendix C: ten family FAQs with candid answers

#set enum(numbering: "1.")

+ *Is this going to steal his novel?*
  Local first means custody by design. The marketing site refuses a hosted factory fantasy.
  The honest work is configuration, discipline, and backups, same as any serious files on disk.

+ *How is this different from typing into Chat Something on a website?*
  Custody and repeatability. A pipeline product aims at manuscripts as artifacts, not disposable chats.

+ *Will it write a bestseller tomorrow?*
  No honest system promises rank. The tool helps finishing and structure. Readers remain the world.

+ *Why does the art look like libraries, desks, and paper?*
  The look is documentary on purpose: writing is a room discipline as much as an idea discipline.

+ *Is one finished long book proof the tool works?*
  It proves a pipeline can be pushed until files exist as a manuscript. It is not proof that anyone else inherits rank or luck without effort.

+ *What should we say at Thanksgiving?*
  He is building publishing infrastructure in a skeptical era. That is enough to be proud of.

+ *Does Mom need to install it?*
  Not unless she wants to. This PDF is the souvenir. If she tries the tool, patience and snacks help.

+ *Why local if cloud is easy?*
  Because easy can cost custody. Novelmate is morally wired the other direction on purpose.

+ *What breaks first?*
  Usually time, GPUs, patience, or a forgotten port. Engineering life.

+ *What is allowed hype?*
  Pride in structure, honesty in limits, love in the room where he works.

